    {
      "questionId": "q5",
      "type": "single",
      "solutionSteps": [
        {
          "step": 1,
          "text": {
            "en": "Write $2\\dfrac{1}{2}$ as $\\dfrac{5}{2}$. Combine the left side over a common denominator: $\\dfrac{x^2 + (x-1)^2}{x(x-1)} = \\dfrac{5}{2}$.",
            "ne": "$2\\dfrac{1}{2}$ लाई $\\dfrac{5}{2}$ मा लेख्नुहोस्। बायाँपट्टिलाई उही हरमा ल्याउँदा: $\\dfrac{x^2 + (x-1)^2}{x(x-1)} = \\dfrac{5}{2}$।"
          }
        },
        {
          "step": 2,
          "text": {
            "en": "Expand the numerator: $x^2 + (x-1)^2 = x^2 + x^2 - 2x + 1 = 2x^2 - 2x + 1$.",
            "ne": "अंशलाई विस्तार गर्दा: $x^2 + (x-1)^2 = x^2 + x^2 - 2x + 1 = 2x^2 - 2x + 1$।"
          }
        },
        {
          "step": 3,
          "text": {
            "en": "Cross-multiply: $2(2x^2 - 2x + 1) = 5x(x-1) \\Rightarrow 4x^2 - 4x + 2 = 5x^2 - 5x$.",
            "ne": "आडा गुणन गर्दा: $2(2x^2 - 2x + 1) = 5x(x-1) \\Rightarrow 4x^2 - 4x + 2 = 5x^2 - 5x$।"
          }
        },
        {
          "step": 4,
          "text": {
            "en": "Simplify: $x^2 - x - 2 = 0 \\Rightarrow (x-2)(x+1) = 0 \\Rightarrow x = 2$ or $x = -1$.",
            "ne": "सरल गर्दा: $x^2 - x - 2 = 0 \\Rightarrow (x-2)(x+1) = 0 \\Rightarrow x = 2$ वा $x = -1$।"
          }
        },
        {
          "step": 5,
          "text": {
            "en": "Since $x \\neq 0$ and $x \\neq 1$ (denominators cannot be zero), both values are valid.",
            "ne": "$x \\neq 0$ र $x \\neq 1$ हुनुपर्ने भएकोले (हर शून्य हुन नहुने), दुवै मान मान्य छन्।"
          }
        }
      ],
      "finalAnswer": {
        "en": "$x = 2, -1$",
        "ne": "$x = 2, -1$"
      },
      "marks": 4
    },
